1
00:01:15,780 --> 00:02:04,100
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,670
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:46,820
What is Alişar Bey talking about for this
long? I hope he's not bothering my Sheikh.

4
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:51,030
If he bothers my father, he would
kindly make him go. Don't you worry.

5
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:13,210
Mother, stop, mother. Don't you
have anyone to help you out?

6
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:17,220
Oh, Alişar Bey, you don't have
to worry about me, thank you.

7
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,820
Help this mother to her home.

8
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,570
May Allah bless you, are
there still people like you?

9
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:28,210
A Bey whose people are not
peaceful, can not have prosperity.

10
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:32,440
- You just don't forget us when you pray.
- May Allah bless you.

11
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:46,070
Listen to me, from now on,
there will be food at noontime.

12
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:50,200
It will be served to the poor
in the marketplace for free.

13
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:03,460
May it be easy, Bala Hatun.

14
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,390
Thank you, Alişar Bey.

15
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:10,930
Mashallah, Mashallah.

16
00:04:11,510 --> 00:04:14,160
You've made such beauties with your hands.

17
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:24,000
Even your one little smile is
a pleasure for me, Bala Hatun.

18
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:27,220
Tawbah!

19
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:53,590
Bala Hatun.

20
00:04:56,090 --> 00:05:00,310
You look the other way,
but I want you to understand.

21
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:05,820
I want you to be the Sultan
of my heart's mansion.

22
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,910
I have the world's most beautiful trouble.

23
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:17,610
But, even being ruined by
your hands is beautiful.

24
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,000
I want you to know...

25
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:26,740
I opened my heart to your
father, he didn't allow it.

26
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,280
But I will wait.

27
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:38,430
A smile, a look will be the seeds
of hope for my garden of union.

28
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:43,510
You are forcing, Alişar Bey. A garden
without consent can't have flowers.

29
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:50,740
I will wait, Bala Hatun.
While I wait, I will say...

30
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:53,520
"Oh, the face of heaven...

31
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,670
"I am so busy with you..."

32
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:59,420
... that I can't even remember myself."

33
00:06:01,050 --> 00:06:07,820
You are going too far, Alişar Bey.
I said my words. There is no beyond.

34
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:27,830
My Bey, we've ruined Gündüz as you
commanded. He should be in the Tent now.

35
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:32,180
Then let's go and say our
best wishes to him.

36
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:38,070
So that they know Alişar Bey's wrath!

37
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,520
Osman.

38
00:06:55,770 --> 00:06:57,470
He is the antichrist.

39
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:01,990
He threw me to the hands of Alişar.

40
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,700
Ma'am, Alişar won't let this go.

41
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:12,430
We've gotten into Alişar's mind
with Master Yannis' help, Helen.

42
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,970
From now on, he will serve us...

43
00:07:18,550 --> 00:07:20,590
... with his every decision.

44
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:26,160
Balances are very fragile.

45
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:29,440
Even a hair's weight matters.

46
00:07:33,330 --> 00:07:37,070
Master Yannis will inform us after
he's done with his calculations.

47
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,820
From now on...

48
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:45,340
... all roads will lead to Abul
for Alişar.

49
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,190
Peace be upon you!

50
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:59,120
Peace be upon you too!

51
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,850
-Sergeant Samsa!
-Osman Bey!

52
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,370
Samsa Bey.

53
00:08:10,850 --> 00:08:12,960
- Sergeant Samsa!
- Konur!

54
00:08:44,810 --> 00:08:45,780
My Bey.

55
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:48,560
People should fear you.

56
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:50,400
You pierced the mountain.

57
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:53,910
Running water wouldn't be in moss.

58
00:08:56,410 --> 00:09:01,070
Osman Bey isn't running,
he's gushing, Mashallah.

59
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:04,210
We are just beginning, brothers.

60
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:09,580
With Allah's help, we will crush
down every obstacle before us.

61
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,800
Inshallah.

62
00:09:21,050 --> 00:09:22,670
Are you hungry, my lion?

63
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:29,190
Here, my Bey.

64
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:33,930
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

65
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:41,490
The first obstacle is Alişar, my Bey.

66
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:54,870
As long as we stand united, back to back,
no one can stand in our way.

67
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:58,440
About Alişar, he must
be close to the Tent.

68
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,640
He's thinking about
getting respect from Kayı.

69
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:07,810
- Come on.
- Sit here, Abdurrahman Gazi.

70
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:44,340
- How is he, Hatun?
- His heart beats slowly.

71
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:49,800
I didn't say it to Ayşe Hatun, but he's
not doing well, my Bey.

72
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:56,400
I took all four arrows, but...

73
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,340
May I come in, my Bey?

74
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,330
Come in.

75
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:10,760
My Bey, Alişar Bey is coming to
our Tent with his soldiers.

76
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:34,510
Alişar will try to threaten the Kayıs.

77
00:11:37,490 --> 00:11:41,180
Dündar Bey will get very angry when
he learns that we took the gold.

78
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:45,020
My uncle's loyalty to Kayı is
out of question.

79
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:48,220
But he lacks caution.

80
00:11:48,730 --> 00:11:50,520
He can't see ahead.

81
00:11:53,270 --> 00:11:58,340
He'll think that we're bandits as well.

82
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,820
But he's not wrong, my Bey.

83
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:08,200
He doesn't know that the gold
is coming from the Mongols.

84
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,770
But he knows that Alişar
is the Mongols' dog.

85
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:15,790
He keeps obeying just so
his system isn't shaken.

86
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:21,360
We'll get through the dirty
traps one by one.

87
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:26,120
We'll take from the cruel, and
give to the poor.

88
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:31,140
Those who rebel against reach prosperity.

89
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:35,070
Now those who obey.

90
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,280
I heard about what happened to Gündüz.

91
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,300
It crushed my heart.

92
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,730
I'm here to say get well.

93
00:13:00,310 --> 00:13:03,480
There was a cruel ambush, Alişar Bey.

94
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,360
How is he doing?

95
00:13:06,590 --> 00:13:08,640
His wounds are deep.

96
00:13:09,570 --> 00:13:12,760
- Who did it?
- We are looking for traces.

97
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,760
We'll figure it out soon.

98
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:22,560
But whoever did this...

99
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:25,740
... will pay a heavy price!

100
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:29,930
Stop talking nonsense, Dündar!
I made them shoot Gündüz!

101
00:13:31,210 --> 00:13:33,750
- You?!
- Stop!

102
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:38,720
Ara you pillaging in my lands,
in my caravansary?

103
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:47,900
We don't pillage, Alişar Bey.
We make a holy war!

104
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:55,610
Since when ambushing and stealing
a holy war, Dündar?

105
00:13:56,730 --> 00:14:02,430
Your betrayal stories are over, and now
are you blaming us with robbery?

106
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:07,310
If stealing the Banner Lord's gold isn't
a robbery, then what is it?

107
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:14,360
A valiant who steals from others,
especially from the Banner Lord...

108
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,730
... can't wear the Kayı's
armour, Alişar Bey!

109
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:23,890
I know each one of their names.

110
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,310
It's Osman's job.

111
00:14:29,310 --> 00:14:31,110
Osman's doings!

112
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,280
Erkut.

113
00:14:41,310 --> 00:14:46,880
Go to the Bazaar. There are people on
Alişar Bey's side, who serve Yannis.

114
00:14:47,510 --> 00:14:51,480
Look sharp and find out who they are.

115
00:14:53,970 --> 00:14:58,410
Yannis' arms are long. We need to
be one step ahead of him.

116
00:14:58,870 --> 00:15:01,300
Otherwise, all our work
will be for nothing.

117
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:04,700
My Bey, do you think he has people
in the caravansary?

118
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:09,040
There are because Alişar knows
that we did it.

119
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:15,240
Then Yannis and Alişar Bey
are cooperating, my Bey.

120
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:19,170
It's too early to declare.

121
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:24,360
But it's certain that they found a way
and surrounded Alişar Bey.

122
00:15:27,350 --> 00:15:31,520
We'll start preparing.
All the equipment is here.

123
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:36,180
Konur brother, you shall bring the news.

124
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:40,380
Check the weapons.

125
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:48,150
We'll enter the castle. We'll take
the gold Alişar Bey wants, and give him.

126
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,110
This is my last warning to Kayıs.

127
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:07,700
If Osman doesn't bring twice the gold
he stole until tomorrow...

128
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:10,160
... all of you will end up like Gündüz!

129
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:16,260
Don't do it, Alişar Bey. How can we get
so much gold in so little time?

130
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:20,270
You touch my pole, and
I'll destroy your Tent!

131
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:23,910
You break by branch, and
I'll burn your mountain!

132
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,810
I'm Alişar Bey! Alişar Bey!

133
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:33,580
Open your ears, and listen carefully.

134
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:38,370
If you don't bring my gold,
just to prove my point...

135
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:45,330
... I'll destroy your Tent, break your
hands, exile your women!

136
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:47,820
Know that!

137
00:17:29,330 --> 00:17:32,070
Kulucahisar. Here, my Bey.

138
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:46,750
Look at Konur. He's been in every
hole like a mole.

139
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:50,980
If Osman Bey didn't make us go there
before, they'd have hunted us like birds.

140
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:23,720
Sofia is alert. They hold everywhere.

141
00:18:23,990 --> 00:18:27,130
My Bey. There's a hole between
the side walls.

142
00:18:27,130 --> 00:18:29,090
We can get in through there.

143
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:35,290
We can get through.
But how will we get inside from there?

144
00:18:37,330 --> 00:18:39,570
What if we use the barrels again, my Bey?

145
00:18:39,570 --> 00:18:42,340
You don't stab the enemy
from the same place, my Baran.

146
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:47,660
I know a secret route.
We can get inside without anyone noticing.

147
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:57,930
You're on a streak, Sıddık.

148
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,620
That secret route won't
be our dungeon, will it?

149
00:19:06,110 --> 00:19:08,560
Sıddık's promise, Osman Bey.

150
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:11,790
I'll take you to the gold.

151
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:31,210
Osman! Look what you did to us!

152
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:36,340
Osman left saying he'd look for traces.
I think he knew Alişar was coming here...

153
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:38,350
... he didn't want to embarrass himself.

154
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:42,660
It's not the first time.
We're out of patience, my Bey!

155
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:46,270
Either tame Osman or exile him!

156
00:19:46,270 --> 00:19:49,080
Or the entire Tent
will disappear because of him!

157
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:51,960
Zöhre! Slow down, you're going too fast!

158
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:54,350
Dündüz is fighting for his life in
the other room.

159
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:59,780
The entire Tent is in danger and you're
still defending Osman!

160
00:19:59,780 --> 00:20:02,570
How many times did Osman not
stand for his word...

161
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,910
... what did he do that he
couldn't explain?

162
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:09,710
Now I'm asking you. Maybe we're hurt,
maybe we'll be hurt more.

163
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:13,150
But if my Osman did something, I'm sure
he knows something!

164
00:20:13,150 --> 00:20:17,100
No, Selcan Hatun!
This can't go on like this!

165
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:22,910
Osman is pushing the limits. He's my
nephew, my life, my blood...

166
00:20:22,910 --> 00:20:28,000
... but if it's either Tent or Osman,
I'll choose the Tent.

167
00:20:31,310 --> 00:20:35,570
His choice.

168
00:21:04,450 --> 00:21:06,440
It shall refresh your heart, my father.

169
00:21:12,910 --> 00:21:15,360
your sorrowful eyes are singing, father.

170
00:21:16,670 --> 00:21:18,730
Your Bala shall die for you.

171
00:21:20,010 --> 00:21:23,190
I remembered the merciful Prophet.

172
00:21:23,990 --> 00:21:30,420
Who knows the pain he feels when
he sees the state of his people.

173
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:36,420
Who knows how much his heart aches.

174
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:44,430
The crusaders, the Mongols spilt
lots of Muslim blood.

175
00:21:45,620 --> 00:21:47,930
They dishonoured us.

176
00:21:49,830 --> 00:21:51,950
They hurt our dignity.

177
00:21:56,240 --> 00:22:01,310
The idea of enslavement rules our hearts.

178
00:22:02,810 --> 00:22:06,980
Especially the things that
invade Muslim hearts...

179
00:22:07,810 --> 00:22:14,990
... grudge, hatred, betrayal, slander...

180
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:17,880
... lust.

181
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:27,050
Oh my Allah!

182
00:22:29,210 --> 00:22:34,400
Who knows how much the state of
his people hurt our Prophet.

183
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:41,690
Did he endure such pain,
such oppression...

184
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,310
... for this?

185
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:52,200
Just so his people could pray
to their Rab in peace...

186
00:22:52,410 --> 00:22:56,780
... did he endure such troubles for this?

187
00:22:59,490 --> 00:23:04,570
Did he sacrifice his friends for this?

188
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:11,120
What about the things Muslims
do to other Muslims?

189
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:17,140
Just because their sects are different,
they slaughter each other.

190
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:22,480
They can't unite against cruelty.

191
00:23:23,310 --> 00:23:30,950
Tomorrow in doomsday, how will we look
at our Prophet's face...

192
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:33,250
... who cried for this people,
my daughter?

193
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,740
How?

194
00:23:55,780 --> 00:23:59,920
What you've said in the
caravansary was right, Abdul.

195
00:24:02,510 --> 00:24:08,470
Now tell me, where did Osman hide my gold?

196
00:24:11,300 --> 00:24:13,340
M-My Bey...

197
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:16,690
He has a secret.

198
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:19,890
We can't see it.

199
00:24:20,890 --> 00:24:24,710
This information is mysterious.

200
00:24:25,090 --> 00:24:28,690
What are you mumbling?
Just say it!

201
00:24:29,250 --> 00:24:34,030
My Bey. The world of spirits!

202
00:25:13,770 --> 00:25:18,460
I see something more valuable
than the gold, my Bey!

203
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:21,390
What is it? Tell me!

204
00:25:21,390 --> 00:25:29,080
Osman's dignity in his Tent is gone!

205
00:25:32,790 --> 00:25:35,110
That's it.

206
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:42,330
There will be more, my Bey!

207
00:25:42,330 --> 00:25:50,370
Your magnificence scares everyone,
your power devours, my Bey!

208
00:25:56,560 --> 00:26:04,540
It's near. There are
big victories on your way!

209
00:26:09,250 --> 00:26:11,110
Continue.

210
00:26:11,450 --> 00:26:15,860
I see the fire, the desire
inside you, my Bey!

211
00:26:19,630 --> 00:26:26,210
To rule! You wish to rule entire lands!

212
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:34,180
Not Sultan's shadow, you wish to
be the Sultan himself!

213
00:26:37,010 --> 00:26:38,980
I do!

214
00:26:41,610 --> 00:26:43,080
Continue!

215
00:26:45,290 --> 00:26:50,740
Woman of the enemy, my Bey! She looks
like your enemy...

216
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:54,730
... but she'll be your best friend!

217
00:26:54,840 --> 00:27:03,220
Your desire is within her. When you unite
with her, she'll give you more power!

218
00:27:05,470 --> 00:27:10,800
Your might will cross the mountains!

219
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,070
Sofia...

220
00:27:59,450 --> 00:28:05,470
In the ninety-nine names of Allah
who has the power to create...

221
00:28:05,670 --> 00:28:08,650
...and who fills our hearts with faith.

222
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,790
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name
of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

223
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:19,530
Kayı's valiant Beys. No point in
beating around the bush.

224
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:24,920
You've all heard about
Alişar Bey's threats.

225
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:32,470
I wanted to consult you so we
could do something about it.

226
00:28:35,340 --> 00:28:40,800
Osman Bey took Alişar Bey's gold. You
employed him as your primary helper.

227
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,990
But as I see, he isn't in the meeting.

228
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:47,030
Why doesn't he explain anything?

229
00:28:47,030 --> 00:28:51,820
This has nothing to do with Osman.
It's all Alişar's doings.

230
00:28:52,010 --> 00:28:57,790
The gold is coming from the Mongols.
But Demirci Bey...

231
00:28:57,790 --> 00:29:02,770
... you don't say anything to Alişar,
but you are questioning Osman.

232
00:29:04,910 --> 00:29:10,090
It's time we unite, and not fight.

233
00:29:12,020 --> 00:29:16,460
We have to collect the amount
Alişar Bey is asking for.

234
00:29:17,610 --> 00:29:20,300
Demirci Bey is talking sense, Bamsı Bey.

235
00:29:20,820 --> 00:29:24,510
If Osman is responsible for this...

236
00:29:24,510 --> 00:29:27,680
... he should bring the gold and rescue
us from this mess.

237
00:29:28,590 --> 00:29:30,620
- He's right!
- He's right.

238
00:29:30,780 --> 00:29:37,250
I believe my nephew handed
the gold out to the poor.

239
00:29:37,450 --> 00:29:42,700
I don't have any hope. None.

240
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:47,060
Then we have to clean Osman's mess again.

241
00:29:48,550 --> 00:29:51,390
We need to do something about Alişar.
Give the order and...

242
00:29:51,390 --> 00:29:54,690
... we shall take battle positions
with my Alps, father.

243
00:29:55,490 --> 00:30:01,190
A possible conflict means we'll be facing
not only Alişar...

244
00:30:01,190 --> 00:30:04,330
... but also the Mongols he's obeying.

245
00:30:04,910 --> 00:30:13,220
Now what we need is to calculate
everything we have that's worth gold.

246
00:30:13,910 --> 00:30:17,710
Everyone should do their part.

247
00:30:17,710 --> 00:30:24,500
I want to know the value of the herd, the
goods in the barn, and the fabrics.

248
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:30,120
If it's necessary, we'll
sell everything...

249
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:35,010
... but we won't let our Tent
be destroyed.

250
00:30:35,010 --> 00:30:37,670
- Thank you.
- Thank you, my Bey.

251
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:08,540
Where's that place you're talking about?
Show me.

252
00:31:09,500 --> 00:31:11,240
Right here.

253
00:31:11,620 --> 00:31:14,210
Behind the walls which protect the castle.

254
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:22,820
Why did you move your eyebrows?
What's on your mind?

255
00:31:23,140 --> 00:31:27,560
Sergeant Samsa. If the infidels made
secret passages for leaving the castle...

256
00:31:27,820 --> 00:31:30,450
... they made traps for those
who try to get in.

257
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:42,190
We're an army of eagles.
We don't fear owls.

258
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:49,270
Instead of being a husband, you look
forward to the battle, Abdurrahman Gazi.

259
00:31:49,770 --> 00:31:55,010
Son, when we came to these lands
behind the scarlet tails...

260
00:31:56,190 --> 00:31:58,120
... we swore on something.

261
00:31:59,210 --> 00:32:06,720
Until the last drop of sweat, the last
drop of blood, the last arrow...

262
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:12,360
...in the quiver, we'll fight for Allah
and be the enemy's nightmare!

263
00:32:14,900 --> 00:32:17,860
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Abdurrahman Gazi.

264
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:47,820
Look what Osman did to us, Selcan Hatun!

265
00:32:49,130 --> 00:32:53,130
We're counting our goods and goats
to pay Alişar's gold.

266
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:57,260
I've been saying it since the beginning,
but you're not listening.

267
00:32:57,260 --> 00:33:01,240
Himself isn't enough, he's going to cause
the whole Tent to be burned!

268
00:33:01,990 --> 00:33:04,040
May I come in, uncle?

269
00:33:04,740 --> 00:33:06,340
Come in!

270
00:33:15,250 --> 00:33:19,850
How can you set your eyes on the
Banner Lord's gold, Osman?

271
00:33:19,850 --> 00:33:26,120
Uncle! Those who are as straight as a die
will manage this homeland...

272
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:29,130
... not those who were spoon-fed.

273
00:33:31,350 --> 00:33:37,090
The gold isn't Alişar's. It's the poor's,
the oppressed's.

274
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:44,170
Alişar came to the Tent and spilt fire!

275
00:33:44,420 --> 00:33:49,580
Gündüz almost died.
Don't you foresee any of these?

276
00:33:49,580 --> 00:33:53,090
If we listened to that tyrant
Alişar's threats...

277
00:33:53,090 --> 00:33:56,000
... we were still sheepherding
in Aleppo, uncle!

278
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,790
Why didn't you come early to
say that to the Banner Lord?

279
00:33:58,970 --> 00:34:02,270
I don't talk with words, I talk
with my sword!

280
00:34:02,270 --> 00:34:05,780
Instructions are yours, actions are
mine, uncle!

281
00:34:07,430 --> 00:34:12,220
Your only action is to get your
uncle in trouble.

282
00:34:15,770 --> 00:34:21,210
I'll take back the Bey's helper duty that
I gave you back!

283
00:34:27,140 --> 00:34:31,900
My loyalty to Kayı is not
limited to duty, Dündar Bey!

284
00:34:38,310 --> 00:34:43,450
We'll see how loyal you are
until tomorrow.

285
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:47,970
But that's the notice
the Banner Lord gave.

286
00:34:48,250 --> 00:34:50,620
Don't worry about your throne.

287
00:34:52,130 --> 00:34:54,680
I'll bring you Alişar's gold.

288
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:11,570
My Osman!

289
00:35:13,980 --> 00:35:18,380
Maybe you are right. But what
you're doing...

290
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:20,290
... isn't right.

291
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:24,720
Don't worry, aunt.

292
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:30,540
You'll pray for me in the future, for
what you're calling a mistake today.

293
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:34,720
I'll go to see my brother.

294
00:36:06,570 --> 00:36:08,140
Aunt.

295
00:36:11,530 --> 00:36:13,660
How's my brother doing?

296
00:36:14,290 --> 00:36:16,210
Bad, Osman.

297
00:36:16,210 --> 00:36:18,400
He didn't wake up yet.

298
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:22,630
My poor Gündüz. Only if he knew
what his brother did.

299
00:36:29,460 --> 00:36:33,690
What has happened, has happened, Zöhre.
Stop making trouble.

300
00:36:33,690 --> 00:36:38,790
Am I wrong? If he knew, would a valiant
like Gündüz be ambushed like that?

301
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:49,210
Gündüz. My Gündüz.

302
00:36:50,160 --> 00:36:53,290
I'm begging you, please.
Open your eyes, Gündüz.

303
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:58,100
Brother!

304
00:37:00,480 --> 00:37:02,210
Brother!

305
00:37:02,210 --> 00:37:04,290
Thankfully!

306
00:37:13,090 --> 00:37:15,170
Osman.

307
00:37:16,220 --> 00:37:18,400
Brother.

308
00:37:22,750 --> 00:37:24,550
Thankfully!

309
00:37:32,230 --> 00:37:37,430
Alişar... Osman... Kayıs...

310
00:37:38,020 --> 00:37:40,790
How are we going to get out of
all this trouble, Princess?

311
00:37:40,790 --> 00:37:44,440
Stars are quite different from
each other, Helen.

312
00:37:47,540 --> 00:37:49,700
Just like people.

313
00:37:54,820 --> 00:37:56,450
Especially Venus.

314
00:37:56,570 --> 00:38:01,760
It's the most magnificent star
of the endless sky.

315
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:08,070
We'll be just like Venus.

316
00:38:15,820 --> 00:38:20,060
While the star dies inside the
darkness we're in...

317
00:38:21,380 --> 00:38:25,500
... we'll glow with the light we
get from the sun just like Venus!

318
00:38:33,890 --> 00:38:35,700
Princess Sofia.

319
00:38:36,330 --> 00:38:40,500
Master Yannis sent some news.
Alişar will be here for the night.

320
00:38:42,330 --> 00:38:44,670
Just like you said, Princess.

321
00:38:45,520 --> 00:38:49,250
The Sun sent it's light to Venus again.

322
00:38:49,250 --> 00:38:51,750
Master Yannis has succeeded.

323
00:38:54,550 --> 00:38:58,260
Then start the preparations.

324
00:38:58,970 --> 00:39:01,470
I don't want anything missing.

325
00:39:03,850 --> 00:39:07,580
It's time to show Alişar Venus'
magnificence.

326
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:09,690
As you say, Princess.

327
00:39:17,360 --> 00:39:21,040
Brother. I have to go.

328
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:25,640
Osman... Brother...

329
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:29,570
These scars won't let me stand up now.

330
00:39:30,270 --> 00:39:35,170
If something happens to you while
I'm like this...

331
00:39:37,640 --> 00:39:39,940
... I'll be very upset. Know that.

332
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:44,090
Don't worry, brother.

333
00:39:45,170 --> 00:39:47,080
Keep calm.

334
00:40:29,140 --> 00:40:31,130
My Osman.

335
00:40:34,010 --> 00:40:37,500
Even the Beys are your enemies now, son.

336
00:40:37,930 --> 00:40:43,300
Don't you worry, Bamsı Bey.
It's time to walk over the enemy.

337
00:40:43,620 --> 00:40:47,090
Thank you, my Osman. The battle is
a valiant's polish.

338
00:40:47,230 --> 00:40:49,080
Otherwise, we'll rust.

339
00:40:49,380 --> 00:40:51,370
To the horses then.

340
00:40:58,270 --> 00:41:00,060
Come here, son.

341
00:41:57,070 --> 00:41:59,660
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

342
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:05,990
We heard about what happened to Gündüz
Bey. We wanted to say get well soon.

343
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:10,170
Thank you. The arrow missed his heart.
He'll be okay.

344
00:42:22,610 --> 00:42:28,390
But the arrows which hit the heart
open the real wounds.

345
00:42:30,910 --> 00:42:35,140
I have a wound in my hear.
It always bleeds.

346
00:42:36,810 --> 00:42:40,990
I won't apply its cure. I'll let it bleed.

347
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:46,080
Both love's wound and pain are beautiful.

348
00:42:48,490 --> 00:42:50,490
I'm waiting, Osman.

349
00:42:50,780 --> 00:42:53,520
You're my home in this world.

350
00:42:55,250 --> 00:43:00,460
I'll give you a lifetime of happiness for
the every second you wait.

351
00:43:03,270 --> 00:43:05,360
Be patient.

352
00:43:07,420 --> 00:43:10,010
Keep praying, darling.

353
00:43:13,580 --> 00:43:17,070
- May Allah protect you.
- You too, Osman.

354
00:43:17,070 --> 00:43:19,260
May Allah protect you.

355
00:43:20,310 --> 00:43:21,870
Go.

356
00:43:56,950 --> 00:43:58,550
Konur Alp.

357
00:43:59,040 --> 00:44:01,700
I've been wanting to ask this for a while.

358
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:04,320
What's with the mark on your eye?

359
00:44:08,990 --> 00:44:11,450
Mongols' work, Sergeant Samsa.

360
00:44:12,890 --> 00:44:14,400
Mongols' work.

361
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:28,290
It healed. But it seems to me
that the pain is still fresh.

362
00:44:30,670 --> 00:44:33,380
What burns my heart is not the pain.

363
00:44:36,160 --> 00:44:38,150
Its the longing of my brother.

364
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:45,910
When Osman Bey rescued me from
the Mongol's slave market...

365
00:44:47,390 --> 00:44:49,360
... my brother was with me.

366
00:44:51,210 --> 00:44:53,380
We were together.

367
00:44:56,620 --> 00:44:59,200
He stayed in their hands.

368
00:45:01,690 --> 00:45:04,760
I did my last move to save him.

369
00:45:07,010 --> 00:45:09,450
Only thing I got was a sword in my eye.

370
00:45:11,470 --> 00:45:14,210
Instead of my eye...

371
00:45:16,290 --> 00:45:18,560
... I wish my brother was with me.

372
00:45:29,390 --> 00:45:33,390
My Konur. Do you know anything about
what happened to your brother?

373
00:45:33,930 --> 00:45:35,730
Did you trace him?

374
00:45:38,790 --> 00:45:42,720
Brother, I say, my Boran. Brother, I say.

375
00:45:45,330 --> 00:45:50,190
I looked at every hole, I wandered
through every single Bazaar.

376
00:45:52,640 --> 00:45:56,890
I look for his smell in every wind,
I say his name every time the sun rises.

377
00:46:19,750 --> 00:46:22,890
We poked your wound for nothing.

378
00:46:25,590 --> 00:46:27,530
Forgive us.

379
00:46:27,820 --> 00:46:32,020
It never healed. It keeps bleeding,
Sergeant Samsa.

380
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:35,550
Keeps bleeding.

381
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:40,720
We're not the sons of the same father.

382
00:46:42,390 --> 00:46:45,500
We're not the same mother's sons, but...

383
00:46:48,490 --> 00:46:52,360
Although we're not brothers by birth,
we're brothers of the same cause.

384
00:46:57,530 --> 00:47:00,180
We're right? We are!

385
00:47:01,620 --> 00:47:05,440
We fight for our cause.
Death behind us.

386
00:47:06,790 --> 00:47:08,750
Our beliefs in front of us.

387
00:47:14,990 --> 00:47:17,630
It's good to have you, brothers.

388
00:47:19,820 --> 00:47:24,670
It's good to have you. Thank you.

389
00:47:35,210 --> 00:47:40,110
I almost died too. You helped me
a lot then, Ayşe Hatun.

390
00:47:40,110 --> 00:47:44,110
You lightened my burden.
May Allah lighten your burden too.

391
00:47:44,960 --> 00:47:48,790
May Allah heal him. He got up, thankfully.

392
00:47:49,040 --> 00:47:51,960
- Get well soon.
- He got well, thankfully.

393
00:47:52,240 --> 00:47:56,240
Thank you. That's nice of you.
You came all the way to here.

394
00:47:56,520 --> 00:47:58,280
May Allah bless you.

395
00:47:59,160 --> 00:48:01,820
They like our Tent a lot, Ayşe Hatun.

396
00:48:03,580 --> 00:48:06,350
They come here on every chance they get.

397
00:48:09,010 --> 00:48:12,130
That's because they know that
they are loved, my Aygül.

398
00:48:12,340 --> 00:48:16,050
Come on, bring some treats for our guests.

399
00:48:17,750 --> 00:48:19,520
Come on!

400
00:48:27,210 --> 00:48:31,680
My father sends his regards too.
He prays for your health.

401
00:48:31,680 --> 00:48:36,160
May Allah bless your Sheikh.
We're very lucky to receive his prayers.

402
00:48:36,160 --> 00:48:42,320
Our Sheikh should pray more, then. But
we can't get our of troubles.

403
00:48:43,190 --> 00:48:45,850
May Allah protect us all.

404
00:49:00,550 --> 00:49:05,920
A young ant saw a pen writing on
a piece of paper, My Akça.

405
00:49:06,560 --> 00:49:11,210
He then told this secret to another ant.

406
00:49:11,620 --> 00:49:16,550
"The pen is a great craftsman.
I saw it myself" he said.

407
00:49:17,050 --> 00:49:22,790
"It engraved sesame flowers and rose
leaves on the paper."

408
00:49:24,850 --> 00:49:27,750
The other ant stopped suddenly.

409
00:49:27,750 --> 00:49:33,750
"The craftsman is not the pencil,
but the fingers." it said.

410
00:49:36,760 --> 00:49:41,270
Another ant who was listening to them
joined the conversation.

411
00:49:42,280 --> 00:49:45,630
"Neither the fingers nor the pencil."

412
00:49:45,630 --> 00:49:49,500
"The real talent is in the arm." it said.

413
00:49:49,700 --> 00:49:54,570
The old ant who was listening to those
three young ant's conversation...

414
00:49:55,280 --> 00:50:01,060
... couldn't hold himself. "Don't look
for talent in the form." He said.

415
00:50:01,060 --> 00:50:06,720
"It's not about the finger, the
arm, or the power." he said.

416
00:50:08,450 --> 00:50:15,120
"What you call power, gives in to a
temporary death when a being sleeps."

417
00:50:17,070 --> 00:50:21,600
"But the mind always lives." it said.

418
00:50:30,790 --> 00:50:34,790
The talent isn't in the wrist, my Akça.

419
00:50:36,400 --> 00:50:38,070
It's in one's mind.

420
00:50:38,640 --> 00:50:40,570
Indeed, my Sheikh.

421
00:50:42,360 --> 00:50:47,780
There are such situations that you can
not get out of them with force.

422
00:50:48,360 --> 00:50:53,720
There are such foes that you can't
beat them with swords.

423
00:50:59,040 --> 00:51:02,530
Alişar is one of those.

424
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:07,000
Against him, we'll stand our
ground with ideas...

425
00:51:07,740 --> 00:51:09,770
... and fight with our minds.

426
00:51:10,920 --> 00:51:14,210
He wants chinas for his mansion.

427
00:51:15,150 --> 00:51:18,930
Sharpen your mind's weapon, and
get to work.

428
00:51:19,820 --> 00:51:24,100
Let's see what you can do.
Gather information, my Akça.

429
00:51:27,590 --> 00:51:31,590
Let's see what games...

430
00:51:31,970 --> 00:51:36,550
... that two-faced Alişar is playing.

431
00:51:37,960 --> 00:51:39,410
Certainly, my Sheikh.

432
00:51:39,410 --> 00:51:44,980
We will not allow those who eat
the enemy's food...

433
00:51:44,980 --> 00:51:50,030
... and try to rule the Muslim
lands, my Akça!

434
00:51:52,290 --> 00:51:56,910
We'll be the minds which
no one can enslave...

435
00:51:58,570 --> 00:52:01,840
... of these troublesome lands
we fought for!

436
00:52:16,240 --> 00:52:18,440
I feel refreshed!

437
00:52:19,210 --> 00:52:23,040
Enjoy your meal, Selcan Hatun.
May it heal you.

438
00:52:26,260 --> 00:52:30,260
Why don't you drink it, Bala Hatun?
Didn't you like it?

439
00:52:42,050 --> 00:52:44,180
It's really nice.

440
00:52:45,350 --> 00:52:48,260
I can taste your hands from
the sherbet, Aygül Hatun.

441
00:52:53,240 --> 00:52:59,000
If you need any medicine or
balm, let us now.

442
00:52:59,160 --> 00:53:01,110
We'll send some with the Dervishes.

443
00:53:01,110 --> 00:53:03,760
My mother can make every medicine.

444
00:53:03,760 --> 00:53:07,910
Only if she could make
something that keeps ticks away.

445
00:53:08,570 --> 00:53:12,220
- Aygül!
- Is that wrong, aunt?

446
00:53:13,590 --> 00:53:18,130
Once a tick gets a hold of you,
it's impossible to get rid of it.

447
00:53:21,500 --> 00:53:24,030
Your words are meaningful, Aylül Hatun.

448
00:53:24,660 --> 00:53:26,490
We understand what you mean.

449
00:53:28,810 --> 00:53:31,960
- We bothered you.
- Not at all, my girl.

450
00:53:31,960 --> 00:53:35,910
- Who are you to bother us?
- Aygül!

451
00:53:41,860 --> 00:53:45,040
You very well know who we are.

452
00:53:46,100 --> 00:53:50,100
So you add salt to our sherbet,
then serve us.

453
00:53:56,260 --> 00:53:57,840
We should leave.

454
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:06,220
We're ready to help, should
you need anything.

455
00:54:06,540 --> 00:54:08,400
Thank you, my girl.

456
00:54:22,010 --> 00:54:25,760
Shame! You're wasting yourself.

457
00:54:26,360 --> 00:54:30,930
Do something about your daughter, Zöhre.
Or I'll have to do it myself!

458
00:54:49,640 --> 00:54:53,630
- Bamsı Bey smelled the battle!
- How couldn't he?

459
00:54:53,630 --> 00:54:56,050
He is an old warrior.

460
00:54:56,050 --> 00:54:57,230
Selamın Aleyküm
(Peace be upon you)

461
00:54:57,230 --> 00:55:00,090
Aleyküm Selam my Bey. Welcome.
(Peace be upon you too)

462
00:55:00,090 --> 00:55:04,660
Thank you. Sergeant Samsa,
is everything ready?

463
00:55:04,660 --> 00:55:06,720
They are, Osman Bey.

464
00:55:09,290 --> 00:55:13,110
Then it's for Allah to decide.

465
00:55:17,100 --> 00:55:21,220
Sıddık! The most important
duty in this battle is yours.

466
00:55:22,180 --> 00:55:26,020
But if you don't want to come, it's okay.

467
00:55:26,020 --> 00:55:31,010
Every sword I swing by you is
my redemption for my past sins.

468
00:55:33,010 --> 00:55:35,820
Don't deny me of this honour, Osman Bey.

469
00:55:38,880 --> 00:55:40,580
Thank you.

470
00:55:43,600 --> 00:55:51,290
My valiant's with Orhun's, Hazar's water
flowing through their veins!

471
00:55:51,780 --> 00:55:54,740
They want to freeze us with
the winter of infidelity...

472
00:55:54,740 --> 00:55:58,450
... and they want to stop us with
their oppression!

473
00:55:59,710 --> 00:56:07,270
Its time we overflow like a river, and
destroy every obstacle in our way!

474
00:56:09,840 --> 00:56:13,850
For the oppressed who reach
the Prophet's...

475
00:56:13,850 --> 00:56:18,030
... level with the wounds
on their hearts...

476
00:56:18,710 --> 00:56:21,060
... for those who wait for the
Turk's justice

477
00:56:21,420 --> 00:56:25,070
For the greatest playmaker!

478
00:56:26,160 --> 00:56:31,790
It's time we destroy the cruel's tricks!

479
00:56:32,150 --> 00:56:37,580
Allahu Ekber!
(Allah is the Greatest)

480
00:56:51,350 --> 00:56:54,200
Is this all, Saltuk Alp?

481
00:56:55,230 --> 00:56:58,420
We could only collect so much
in these hard times, my Bey.

482
00:56:58,420 --> 00:57:02,820
Don't worry. If Osman said he'll find
those golds, he will find them.

483
00:57:03,140 --> 00:57:07,410
Should we trust Osman with the entire
Tent's future, Selcan Hatun?

484
00:57:07,650 --> 00:57:09,630
Should we sit here with our hands tied?

485
00:57:09,630 --> 00:57:15,430
Our hands are not tied. Bowing to that
dog called Alişar is against our laws!

486
00:57:21,180 --> 00:57:24,290
Let's cover the golds with poison
and then give them.

487
00:57:24,800 --> 00:57:27,590
Stop, Selcan Hatun!

488
00:57:28,240 --> 00:57:35,400
He's a Turk Bey. If they learn that we do
this, the Mongols will be on to us.

489
00:57:36,700 --> 00:57:39,360
What if Osman can't bring the gold?

490
00:57:39,570 --> 00:57:43,150
Then Allah knows what we'll do.

491
00:58:53,520 --> 00:58:56,160
There are always guards up ahead.

492
00:58:57,730 --> 00:58:59,420
Go then.

493
00:59:00,540 --> 00:59:02,390
They probably missed you.

494
00:59:36,550 --> 00:59:37,940
Who are you?

495
00:59:43,310 --> 00:59:44,780
Traitor Salvador!

496
00:59:45,370 --> 00:59:48,630
I ran out of the Turks' hands.
I'm here to take shelter.

497
00:59:53,550 --> 00:59:56,400
My Bey. Should we go?

498
00:59:56,770 --> 00:59:58,510
We should stay, brother.

499
00:59:59,680 --> 01:00:01,860
Sıddık knows what to do.

500
01:00:50,770 --> 01:00:55,280
Stop robbing the dead!
You're a Muslim, Sıddık!

501
01:01:05,380 --> 01:01:07,270
Here's the hatch, Osman Bey.

502
01:01:07,270 --> 01:01:10,720
After the hatch, there's a secret
door to the treasure room.

503
01:01:14,180 --> 01:01:17,100
- Where does this lead to?
- To the governor's room.

504
01:01:17,100 --> 01:01:19,600
It's for him to get away if
there's a siege.

505
01:01:19,600 --> 01:01:21,650
Why didn't you tell us in the beginning?

506
01:01:28,160 --> 01:01:30,960
You guys continue, Bamsı Bey.

507
01:01:30,960 --> 01:01:35,560
If this leads to the governor's room,
I should say hi to Sofia.

508
01:01:35,560 --> 01:01:38,780
My Osman, I should come with you.

509
01:01:38,780 --> 01:01:43,000
Your duty is more important, Bamsı Bey.
Take the gold.

510
01:01:44,640 --> 01:01:47,200
- We'll meet here.
- Thank you, Osman.

511
01:01:57,660 --> 01:02:00,510
I should lead the way, there
might be traps.

512
01:02:01,580 --> 01:02:05,580
Why didn't you tell Osman Bey
that there would be traps?

513
01:02:06,780 --> 01:02:10,130
That's the governor's way.
There are no traps there.

514
01:02:13,010 --> 01:02:16,270
Lead the way, Sıddık. Let's go.

515
01:03:42,280 --> 01:03:47,230
Alişar Bey, welcome. Princess Sofia
is waiting for you. Here.

516
01:04:03,130 --> 01:04:05,830
Here's the secret entrance of
the treasure room.

517
01:04:10,110 --> 01:04:12,250
Is there anyone inside?

518
01:04:12,610 --> 01:04:16,140
There's no one inside.
But there are guards at the door.

519
01:04:16,140 --> 01:04:19,500
- How many?
- I don't know.

520
01:04:19,830 --> 01:04:23,350
It's a huge castle's treasure
room after all.

521
01:04:28,630 --> 01:04:31,720
Sıddık! You're sure, right?

522
01:04:32,870 --> 01:04:36,930
You're not leading us to
the dungeon, are you?

523
01:04:36,930 --> 01:04:39,330
No. I'm sure.

524
01:04:42,630 --> 01:04:45,210
I'm your son now, Bamsı Bey.

525
01:04:47,040 --> 01:04:49,070
Say the word and I'll die for you!

526
01:04:51,970 --> 01:04:55,770
You blessed me with bravery.
May you live long.

527
01:04:57,020 --> 01:05:00,690
May Allah bless you in this
world and the afterlife.

528
01:05:02,520 --> 01:05:03,880
Let's go.

529
01:05:49,930 --> 01:05:54,710
Alişar Bey. Welcome.
Here.

530
01:06:05,210 --> 01:06:10,190
While I escape from the dungeon and hardly
save my life, you come to my castle...

531
01:06:11,980 --> 01:06:14,200
... to be honest, it is great courage

532
01:06:19,700 --> 01:06:21,530
You underestimate me Sofia.

533
01:06:22,020 --> 01:06:23,300
I am Alişar Bey.

534
01:06:24,920 --> 01:06:28,770
I came here to lay the foundations of
an unshakeable alliance.

535
01:06:30,120 --> 01:06:32,640
After being deceived by Osman's words?

536
01:07:04,700 --> 01:07:07,250
Be quiet.
The guards might hear us.

537
01:07:30,300 --> 01:07:32,780
While their people are hungry...

538
01:07:32,780 --> 01:07:34,510
... they swim in gold.

539
01:07:43,500 --> 01:07:45,640
Your mother raised you well.

540
01:07:48,140 --> 01:07:51,720
My little lion.

541
01:08:00,700 --> 01:08:01,890
What was that sound?

542
01:08:02,100 --> 01:08:03,870
Theo go check on the room.

543
01:08:10,460 --> 01:08:12,130
Come on valiants, come on.

544
01:08:28,290 --> 01:08:31,080
Open the door. Thieves!
Open the door!

545
01:08:31,130 --> 01:08:35,540
Come on, sons! We can't lose time.
Let's carry these!

546
01:08:36,520 --> 01:08:38,420
Let's carry these all together.

547
01:08:41,420 --> 01:08:43,780
Soldiers, there are thieves!
Open the door!

548
01:08:44,070 --> 01:08:45,280
Open the door!

549
01:08:47,660 --> 01:08:48,590
Soldiers!

550
01:08:49,390 --> 01:08:50,460
Hurry up!

551
01:08:56,150 --> 01:08:57,500
Open the door!

552
01:09:00,990 --> 01:09:03,360
Open the door! I said open the door!

553
01:09:14,790 --> 01:09:15,520
Soldiers!

554
01:09:16,030 --> 01:09:16,730
Soldiers!

555
01:09:17,160 --> 01:09:18,960
Take this one too, my son.

556
01:09:19,490 --> 01:09:20,700
Open the door!

557
01:09:34,870 --> 01:09:37,870
We both know all I said is true.

558
01:09:41,440 --> 01:09:45,440
Coming here while you know that shows
you are taking every single risk.

559
01:09:49,130 --> 01:09:50,760
Isn't it worth it?

560
01:09:50,760 --> 01:09:52,730
Of course, it's worth it Alisar Bey...

561
01:09:53,400 --> 01:09:55,910
But I'm the servant of the Byzantine...

562
01:09:55,910 --> 01:09:59,240
... you're the servant of the Seljuks
under the siege of the Mongols.

563
01:10:02,510 --> 01:10:07,040
We are both passionate enough to not
depend on anyone, Sofia.

564
01:10:07,640 --> 01:10:09,150
This is another fact...

565
01:10:10,900 --> 01:10:14,900
... however, there is an obstacle in the
path of our alliance.

566
01:10:16,440 --> 01:10:17,980
For example?

567
01:10:18,440 --> 01:10:20,200
For example, Kayıs.

568
01:10:21,380 --> 01:10:23,110
For example, Edebali.

569
01:10:29,290 --> 01:10:32,730
Open the door! Thieves!

570
01:10:49,760 --> 01:10:52,230
Open the door!

571
01:11:04,020 --> 01:11:05,880
You don't have to carry another one.

572
01:11:05,960 --> 01:11:07,720
There are still lots of them, Sıddık.

573
01:11:09,050 --> 01:11:10,880
This is enough for me.

574
01:11:12,300 --> 01:11:14,140
It is time to close the door.

575
01:11:22,730 --> 01:11:23,690
Sıddık!

576
01:11:24,660 --> 01:11:25,570
Sıddık!

577
01:11:26,090 --> 01:11:27,530
Where are you? Open the hatch!

578
01:11:31,540 --> 01:11:32,550
Sıddık!

579
01:11:34,340 --> 01:11:35,830
It's the end of the road, Turk!

580
01:11:36,260 --> 01:11:38,510
You all filthy Turks are going to die!

581
01:11:38,650 --> 01:11:40,310
Osman Bey did nothing wrong to you!

582
01:11:41,820 --> 01:11:43,060
Open the hatch now!

583
01:11:43,060 --> 01:11:45,560
You filthy Turks are so naive.

584
01:11:45,910 --> 01:11:47,490
Say hi to Osman Bey!

585
01:11:47,770 --> 01:11:52,210
I am going to kill you Sıddık!
I'll eat you alive!

586
01:12:00,220 --> 01:12:02,810
Though Kayıs are in the control of Söğüt...

587
01:12:03,050 --> 01:12:05,750
...they are only a simple Tent that
belongs to me.

588
01:12:07,470 --> 01:12:11,470
When it comes to Edebali, however,
I don't know why you are scared of him.

589
01:12:13,350 --> 01:12:16,330
He is just a simple merchant in my Bazaar.

590
01:12:17,050 --> 01:12:18,060
That's it.

591
01:12:19,570 --> 01:12:23,570
You also underestimate us, Alişar Bey.

592
01:12:27,120 --> 01:12:32,000
Yes, you are right.
Kayıs are only a simple Tent...

593
01:12:33,040 --> 01:12:37,300
...yet, they are the most important
warriors of the Turks in these lands...

594
01:12:37,300 --> 01:12:39,110
...who are constantly on our path.

595
01:12:39,340 --> 01:12:44,440
And Edebali is only a tout who taunts the
Turks against us.

596
01:12:45,710 --> 01:12:49,210
Being a merchant is only a mask for him.

597
01:12:49,720 --> 01:12:57,450
If you want a strong alliance as you like,
you need to eliminate these two threats.

598
01:13:04,370 --> 01:13:09,460
I need the Ahis and Edebali for economical
benefits.

599
01:13:11,440 --> 01:13:15,440
And, the Kayıs, right now, are busy with
collecting the golds they stole from me.

600
01:13:19,510 --> 01:13:24,850
Alisar Bey, then why are the Mongols
are coming?

601
01:13:32,920 --> 01:13:38,530
I see you are well aware of
every kind of information, Princess.

602
01:13:40,430 --> 01:13:43,090
We also have our own birds, Alişar Bey.

603
01:13:43,840 --> 01:13:47,840
As you know, the greatest power that
exists is to have information.

604
01:13:49,360 --> 01:13:53,910
You are right. The Mongol commander and
his soldiers...

605
01:13:53,910 --> 01:13:57,140
...will be at Söğüt by the morning.

606
01:13:58,150 --> 01:14:01,310
I'll then see how Kayıs behave.

607
01:14:02,520 --> 01:14:06,190
Alişar!

608
01:14:16,100 --> 01:14:20,100
To our alliance, Alişar Bey.

609
01:14:35,520 --> 01:14:36,720
Traitor dog!

610
01:14:39,620 --> 01:14:43,450
Bamsı Bey! Sıddık has just
closed the hatch!

611
01:14:44,060 --> 01:14:46,180
Traitor dog!

612
01:14:53,980 --> 01:14:56,640
Hold on, Bamsı Bey. Hold on!

613
01:14:56,810 --> 01:15:00,170
We need to leave this place as soon as
possible.

614
01:15:00,740 --> 01:15:05,480
Brother Boran, go to the capsule at once
and try to open it. We need to leave.

615
01:15:06,390 --> 01:15:09,300
With the power of Allah, Bamsı Bey.
Let's go!

616
01:15:22,840 --> 01:15:25,890
Open the damn door!

617
01:15:26,850 --> 01:15:29,910
I hope our alliance brings luck to
both of us.

618
01:15:31,160 --> 01:15:33,360
I have no doubts about that.

619
01:15:34,070 --> 01:15:36,950
Our solidarity will be so strong.

620
01:15:38,410 --> 01:15:41,360
Let me escort you to your room.

621
01:15:41,950 --> 01:15:47,480
Princess, I'm sorry to say that I won't
spend the night here.

622
01:15:47,720 --> 01:15:51,390
I need to be present at Tent in the
morning.

623
01:16:09,270 --> 01:16:13,270
Let my soldiers escort you to the exit.

624
01:16:14,170 --> 01:16:15,840
Have a good night, Princess.

625
01:16:15,970 --> 01:16:16,830
Good night.

626
01:16:34,080 --> 01:16:35,690
Traitor dog!

627
01:16:42,420 --> 01:16:46,420
Open the damn door. Thieves!

628
01:16:49,030 --> 01:16:53,030
The door won't stand for too long,
Abdurrahman Gazi. You should get inside.

629
01:17:36,800 --> 01:17:40,800
Bamsı Bey, we can't get the door open.

630
01:17:45,640 --> 01:17:48,240
Bring the spearhead!

631
01:18:04,660 --> 01:18:07,320
Make way! Make way!

632
01:18:38,020 --> 01:18:45,900
My sons! My valiants! Today is the day we
unite with Allah!

633
01:18:47,790 --> 01:18:49,570
Give your last blessings!

634
01:18:50,060 --> 01:18:52,810
May Allah be with us!

635
01:19:00,070 --> 01:19:02,070
Come on, Valiants!

636
01:19:10,970 --> 01:19:12,500
My brothers!

637
01:19:13,680 --> 01:19:14,660
My Osman!

638
01:19:14,860 --> 01:19:16,260
My Bamsı Bey!

639
01:19:17,060 --> 01:19:18,590
Sergeant Samsa!

640
01:19:21,620 --> 01:19:23,350
Magnificent!

641
01:19:23,530 --> 01:19:26,070
Come on! Come on, valiants!

642
01:19:29,100 --> 01:19:31,430
Hold on Valiants! Hold on!

643
01:19:32,600 --> 01:19:35,530
It's good to see you again my Bey!

644
01:19:36,620 --> 01:19:38,050
Konur!

645
01:20:05,580 --> 01:20:06,890
My Osman!

646
01:20:07,370 --> 01:20:08,670
Bamsı Bey!

647
01:20:16,780 --> 01:20:18,190
How could this be?

648
01:20:18,190 --> 01:20:20,630
Who could get into the treasure room like
this?

649
01:20:20,630 --> 01:20:22,910
No way! A secret passage?

650
01:20:23,230 --> 01:20:24,330
Salvador.

651
01:20:25,530 --> 01:20:27,710
It can be nobody but Salvador!

652
01:20:28,230 --> 01:20:31,010
He cooperated with Osman and took
all of our gold.

653
01:20:34,860 --> 01:20:36,280
Here you go.

654
01:20:49,550 --> 01:20:51,890
Brother Abdurrahman, let's go.

655
01:21:03,230 --> 01:21:04,440
Go.

656
01:21:17,610 --> 01:21:21,610
With more force, come on!

657
01:21:34,470 --> 01:21:36,010
Well done.

658
01:21:37,490 --> 01:21:40,750
Sergeant Samsa! Let's go!

659
01:22:23,010 --> 01:22:27,010
Hurry up! We need to get them!

660
01:22:33,110 --> 01:22:37,120
They are downstairs! Go! Get Them! Quick!

661
01:22:43,910 --> 01:22:47,270
My Osman, Salvador betrayed us.

662
01:22:48,020 --> 01:22:50,710
Sıddık has never been Sıddık at all.

663
01:22:52,360 --> 01:22:54,560
One day, we will get revenge, Bamsı Bey.

664
01:23:13,660 --> 01:23:15,780
Let's go!

665
01:23:26,520 --> 01:23:27,540
Damn it!

666
01:23:28,570 --> 01:23:30,890
Are we going to tell this about
Alişar Bey?

667
01:23:31,480 --> 01:23:35,070
For what, so that he can mock us? Never.

668
01:23:36,160 --> 01:23:38,040
He won't know about this.

669
01:23:40,630 --> 01:23:42,500
Follow them!

670
01:23:42,500 --> 01:23:47,910
Then, destroy the passage and let nobody
get inside of this room ever again.

671
01:24:55,990 --> 01:24:59,020
I knew he would do that all along.

672
01:24:59,040 --> 01:25:01,320
That traitor dog!

673
01:25:09,460 --> 01:25:11,450
How many chests are missing?

674
01:25:11,570 --> 01:25:13,700
Three chests are missing, Samsa Bey.

675
01:25:15,000 --> 01:25:17,780
This is still enough for Alişar...

676
01:25:18,720 --> 01:25:20,780
... but we are short on loot.

677
01:25:21,490 --> 01:25:23,770
I was planning to buy new tents.

678
01:25:26,540 --> 01:25:30,090
Don't worry. We will get them
after the next raid, Sergeant Samsa.

679
01:25:30,830 --> 01:25:33,020
I will give some of my shares to you.

680
01:25:33,570 --> 01:25:39,290
After all, Sergeant Samsa's Tent
is our Tent.

681
01:25:45,630 --> 01:25:50,700
With the help of Allah, from tents, we
will move to homes made of stones.

682
01:25:50,700 --> 01:25:52,510
One side of me is thinking about that.

683
01:25:52,510 --> 01:25:54,790
The castle is right here, Konur.

684
01:25:56,310 --> 01:25:59,720
By the way, when are we going to capture
this castle, Osman Bey?

685
01:26:00,230 --> 01:26:04,390
I've been dreaming of conquering for
a while. It's a piece of cake.

686
01:26:06,450 --> 01:26:09,060
Its time will come eventually.

687
01:26:14,300 --> 01:26:16,890
He said I'm a Muslim now.

688
01:26:17,700 --> 01:26:19,540
Recited the shahadah.

689
01:26:21,820 --> 01:26:25,460
He said he'd be my son. He promised me.

690
01:26:32,900 --> 01:26:38,030
He tricked us, Samsa Bey. We will get our
revenge soon.

691
01:26:38,310 --> 01:26:41,050
I freed the murderer of my own son.

692
01:26:43,330 --> 01:26:50,530
I'm the one who tricked myself and for
that I should be ashamed.

693
01:26:56,790 --> 01:26:59,190
There is hope after every incident, Bamsı
Bey.

694
01:26:59,890 --> 01:27:01,800
The time will come.

695
01:27:07,730 --> 01:27:12,220
However, I have bad news for you.

696
01:27:14,880 --> 01:27:16,790
What is it, my Bey?

697
01:27:21,770 --> 01:27:23,520
The Mongols.

698
01:27:26,610 --> 01:27:28,430
What about them, my son?

699
01:27:29,420 --> 01:27:31,640
I heard it while Sofia was talking.

700
01:27:31,700 --> 01:27:33,860
The Mongolians will come to
Söğüt, she said.

701
01:27:34,520 --> 01:27:40,110
After we deal with Alişar, we'll go to
Söğüt to find out what they want.

702
01:27:44,400 --> 01:27:46,450
Let's go.

703
01:28:27,330 --> 01:28:28,980
Princess Sofia.

704
01:28:35,360 --> 01:28:37,360
Please listen to me Princess Sofia.

705
01:28:51,810 --> 01:28:54,340
Despicable dog.

706
01:28:57,190 --> 01:29:00,020
Nothing is as you think.

707
01:29:06,700 --> 01:29:08,190
Traitor.

708
01:29:11,910 --> 01:29:14,690
You stabbed me in the back at
Alişar Bey's mansion.

709
01:29:18,150 --> 01:29:25,840
You told Osman Bey about the secret
passages to treasury room.

710
01:29:30,430 --> 01:29:31,390
No!

711
01:29:34,330 --> 01:29:37,330
They already had the plans of the castle!

712
01:29:40,060 --> 01:29:41,950
How?

713
01:29:43,210 --> 01:29:45,510
Answer my question, you dog!

714
01:29:47,120 --> 01:29:47,970
Edabali.

715
01:29:49,270 --> 01:29:53,540
In order to save my own life, I made them
believe that I became a Muslim.

716
01:29:54,350 --> 01:29:57,950
I infiltrated them and made them trust me.

717
01:29:58,390 --> 01:30:00,840
I didn't have any other options.

718
01:30:01,900 --> 01:30:05,900
I didn't betray master Yannis.

719
01:30:06,740 --> 01:30:11,400
If I wanted, I could just kill your
soldiers and run away with the golds.

720
01:30:22,510 --> 01:30:24,390
Is this true?

721
01:30:24,810 --> 01:30:28,810
Yes, it is true, my Princess. He saved
our lives by pretending to be killing us.

722
01:30:28,940 --> 01:30:31,590
Then he handed us the gold.

723
01:30:39,510 --> 01:30:40,810
They are coming!

724
01:30:40,810 --> 01:30:43,980
You should play dead. And you run away.
Trust me.

725
01:31:00,540 --> 01:31:03,500
In the name of our holy mother Mary, I'm
telling you the truth.

726
01:31:03,860 --> 01:31:06,470
I have a lot to tell you about Osman.

727
01:31:24,890 --> 01:31:26,570
Here you go.

728
01:31:54,070 --> 01:31:56,410
Would you like me to prepare a meal,
my Bey?

729
01:32:01,850 --> 01:32:05,840
Give me the biggest and the most beautiful
room you got.

730
01:32:06,020 --> 01:32:07,700
As you wish, my Bey.

731
01:32:07,700 --> 01:32:09,530
Follow me.

732
01:34:11,180 --> 01:34:19,030
There will be no piece of land where the
shadow of Genghis Khan can't reach.

733
01:34:27,070 --> 01:34:35,010
The legacy of our ancestors will continue
with us.

734
01:34:35,660 --> 01:34:44,530
Let the Kayıs and Alps be forsaken
forever.

735
01:34:46,870 --> 01:34:52,640
Without soul, flesh, humiliated

736
01:34:53,330 --> 01:34:58,280
Tomorrow we'll attack all their Tents and
make suji from their blood...

737
01:34:58,280 --> 01:35:00,390
... boots from their skins...

738
01:35:00,390 --> 01:35:03,770
... jewellery from their honour.

739
01:35:06,700 --> 01:35:10,640
Tomorrow, I want the Tent's Beys.

740
01:35:11,310 --> 01:35:15,590
And Söğüt.

741
01:35:16,140 --> 01:35:20,140
Don't forget every Turk means
twelve gold of tax.

742
01:35:20,760 --> 01:35:24,760
It'd be stupid to slay a
golden egg-laying chickens.

743
01:35:25,570 --> 01:35:29,080
Don't forget why you're here.

744
01:35:29,880 --> 01:35:35,360
To the entertainment and booty!

745
01:35:38,140 --> 01:35:42,140
To the entertainment and booty!

746
01:36:03,040 --> 01:36:06,910
Alişar Bey is probably all over
Kayı Tent now.

747
01:36:07,010 --> 01:36:11,010
I'll keep him in my hands.

748
01:36:12,020 --> 01:36:17,230
And when my job is done...

749
01:36:18,360 --> 01:36:20,150
... I'll strangle him.

750
01:36:26,620 --> 01:36:29,520
- May I come in?
- Come in.

751
01:36:35,670 --> 01:36:39,220
Master. Akça Dervish is here.
Ahis are with him.

752
01:36:39,220 --> 01:36:41,250
Akça Dervish?

753
01:37:06,960 --> 01:37:08,540
Akça Dervish?

754
01:37:09,860 --> 01:37:13,860
What brought you
to Alişar Bey's mansion?

755
01:37:14,410 --> 01:37:19,600
Our Sheikh ordered. Alişar Bey wanted
to cover his mansion's walls with chinas.

756
01:37:19,950 --> 01:37:21,970
I'm here to examine.

757
01:37:22,590 --> 01:37:24,230
Chinas...

758
01:37:38,580 --> 01:37:40,520
Here. Continue.

759
01:38:10,540 --> 01:38:12,950
Time's up, Dündar Bey!

760
01:38:14,030 --> 01:38:16,280
Tell me. Where's my gold?

761
01:38:16,700 --> 01:38:21,740
The Tent is Kayı's, but the
judgement is yours, Alişar Bey.

762
01:38:22,070 --> 01:38:26,070
Be calm. I'll tell you everything.

763
01:38:35,060 --> 01:38:37,050
Akça Dervish!

764
01:38:37,800 --> 01:38:39,930
Why are you leaving
without saying anything?

765
01:38:40,210 --> 01:38:43,480
Take this gift from Alişar Bey to
Sheikh Edebali.

766
01:38:43,990 --> 01:38:45,540
Thank you.

767
01:39:06,950 --> 01:39:08,780
Take them away.

768
01:39:41,320 --> 01:39:43,230
What's going on here?

769
01:39:47,440 --> 01:39:49,170
Talk now.

770
01:39:50,850 --> 01:39:52,590
I'm listening.

771
01:39:55,530 --> 01:39:58,850
We couldn't gather enough
gold, Alişar Bey.

772
01:39:59,800 --> 01:40:03,970
However, I checked all of our finance.

773
01:40:03,990 --> 01:40:09,320
We are ready to give away all our herds
and rugs.

774
01:40:10,890 --> 01:40:14,760
What can I make out of your useless rugs?

775
01:40:15,690 --> 01:40:20,380
I am talking about gold, Dündar Bey.
Gold!

776
01:40:20,780 --> 01:40:25,780
Didn't I tell you to I'd come and burn
your tribe?

777
01:40:26,760 --> 01:40:32,730
Who can stop me now when I set the stakes
in the middle of the tribe?

778
01:40:32,730 --> 01:40:36,880
And empale your alps?
Who can stop me?

779
01:40:38,600 --> 01:40:42,720
What if I throw you into the
boiling caldrons?

780
01:40:42,800 --> 01:40:46,490
And rip out your lungs?

781
01:40:46,490 --> 01:40:50,340
Who will stop me, Dündar?
Who!?

782
01:40:55,290 --> 01:40:57,120
Osman.

783
01:41:55,790 --> 01:41:57,160
Alişar Bey.

784
01:41:57,460 --> 01:41:59,330
Your gold is outside.

785
01:42:03,210 --> 01:42:04,930
Now leave my tribe alone.

786
01:42:05,480 --> 01:42:07,630
Where are you going without my word?

787
01:42:17,120 --> 01:42:18,710
I kept my promise.

788
01:42:19,360 --> 01:42:21,830
I don't need permission from
anyone to leave.

789
01:42:24,390 --> 01:42:26,940
I am not anyone, Osman.

790
01:42:27,380 --> 01:42:29,320
I am the banner lord.

791
01:42:33,090 --> 01:42:35,070
Will you stop me?

792
01:42:39,360 --> 01:42:41,930
When I say "stop" in this country...

793
01:42:42,190 --> 01:42:45,710
even rain and wind stops.

794
01:42:46,140 --> 01:42:48,010
You'll stop, too Osman!

795
01:42:49,210 --> 01:42:51,650
Stop me if you can!

796
01:42:51,650 --> 01:42:54,900
- Osman!
- Alişar Bey!

797
01:42:58,760 --> 01:43:00,690
Don't go mad.

798
01:43:03,230 --> 01:43:05,370
Osman.

799
01:43:16,240 --> 01:43:23,050
From now on, you can't rule where
I am standing, Alişar Bey.

800
01:43:33,180 --> 01:43:37,930
You shouldn't have disobeyed the
banner lord, Osman.

801
01:43:42,380 --> 01:43:47,720
You are not being a Bey,
at least be an uncle.

802
01:43:47,800 --> 01:43:52,020
Talk it through with Osman.

803
01:43:52,960 --> 01:43:57,670
Otherwise, this will end with blood.

804
01:43:58,690 --> 01:44:00,330
Blood.

805
01:44:06,470 --> 01:44:10,830
From now, nothing will be like before.

806
01:44:11,720 --> 01:44:13,620
Be aware of this.

807
01:44:28,360 --> 01:44:31,260
What does this Alişar mean, father?

808
01:44:32,510 --> 01:44:38,340
Huge trouble is approaching, son.
Huge trouble.

809
01:46:19,340 --> 01:46:21,040
I am hungry.

810
01:46:26,250 --> 01:46:28,560
Thank you.
Thank you.

811
01:49:36,150 --> 01:49:37,820
Today...

812
01:49:38,530 --> 01:49:43,560
We take revenge.

813
01:49:43,900 --> 01:49:46,310
Today...

814
01:49:47,080 --> 01:49:52,440
We sacrifice for our ancestors.

815
01:49:53,960 --> 01:49:56,480
Today...

816
01:49:57,680 --> 01:50:04,180
We receive the mighty light from the sun.

817
01:50:05,260 --> 01:50:07,800
Today...

818
01:50:08,620 --> 01:50:11,580
We take the Turks'...

819
01:50:12,250 --> 01:50:17,310
joy of life, power...

820
01:50:18,320 --> 01:50:20,970
faith...

821
01:50:21,730 --> 01:50:25,980
from their hands!

822
01:50:26,530 --> 01:50:28,880
Today...

823
01:50:29,000 --> 01:50:32,460
is the day of Balga...

824
01:50:32,460 --> 01:50:36,260
who shapes in flesh and bones...

825
01:50:36,360 --> 01:50:39,820
with Cengiz Han's blood.

826
01:50:45,870 --> 01:50:52,900
Now, go everywhere and tell Balgay's
words.

827
01:50:54,500 --> 01:51:00,390
I came here to impose tax on this land...

828
01:51:00,430 --> 01:51:05,320
enough to make sculpture of me and my
soldiers.

829
01:51:07,420 --> 01:51:09,270
Or...

830
01:51:10,950 --> 01:51:17,500
to take your kids, your wives...

831
01:51:19,820 --> 01:51:22,320
your lives!

832
01:51:24,600 --> 01:51:28,900
Mark my words!

833
01:51:49,100 --> 01:51:53,810
You kept talking about Osman, look
how he brought the gold, Zöhre.

834
01:51:53,870 --> 01:51:58,520
Osman shows us the worst thing first,
then he convinces us to the bad.

835
01:51:58,520 --> 01:52:01,350
- Is this good.
- It is.

836
01:52:01,420 --> 01:52:04,710
Think about what would've happened if
Osman had not been there.

837
01:52:04,730 --> 01:52:08,030
Hatuns. stop quarreling.

838
01:52:08,090 --> 01:52:11,600
Thank Allah, we got over this trouble.

839
01:52:11,680 --> 01:52:13,460
Thank Allah.

840
01:52:32,940 --> 01:52:34,910
What is this noise, uncle?

841
01:52:37,760 --> 01:52:40,550
Father.
It's Mongols.

842
01:53:36,060 --> 01:53:39,020
So, that's what Alişar meant.

843
01:53:57,180 --> 01:53:59,940
I swear on Cengiz.

844
01:54:00,060 --> 01:54:05,780
I swear on the souls in the sky.

845
01:54:05,880 --> 01:54:11,430
If you resists, I'll even kill your
babies.

846
01:54:16,510 --> 01:54:21,980
This country is Mongol's iron fist
Balgay's.

847
01:54:23,860 --> 01:54:27,090
Söğüt is Kayıs'!

848
01:54:28,560 --> 01:54:30,220
Boğaç!

849
01:54:46,740 --> 01:54:48,470
Boğaç!

850
01:54:50,470 --> 01:54:53,460
Boğaç! Boğaç!
Brother!

851
01:54:53,460 --> 01:54:58,220
Whoever resist us deserves to die!

852
01:55:20,610 --> 01:55:24,890
I brought you Mongol's martial...

853
01:55:25,670 --> 01:55:29,610
and unending anger.

854
01:55:33,390 --> 01:55:35,620
Dündar...

855
01:55:35,650 --> 01:55:39,040
From now on, you are not a banner lord.

856
01:55:39,320 --> 01:55:42,130
You are just a herd boy, Dündar.

857
01:55:48,080 --> 01:55:53,150
You'll come into Commander Balgay's
presence with Gündüz.

858
01:56:15,520 --> 01:56:19,060
We have brought the Beys who didn't pay
enough taxes, sir.

859
01:56:51,780 --> 01:56:54,890
Aren't we going to participate in the
feast, Commander Balgay?

860
01:56:55,780 --> 01:57:02,600
The feast is going to start when Osman
and his fellas fall into my hands.

861
01:57:31,050 --> 01:57:32,280
Enchain them!

862
01:58:17,790 --> 01:58:20,540
- Zöhre!
- Mother.

863
01:58:30,130 --> 01:58:37,510
The souls in the sky and underground gave
us everything.

864
01:58:39,440 --> 01:58:44,200
The only thing they didn't give to us is
the feeling of mercy.

865
01:58:44,620 --> 01:58:46,530
Aunt!

866
01:58:53,930 --> 01:58:55,860
Take them!

867
01:59:13,460 --> 01:59:15,180
Father.

868
01:59:54,770 --> 01:59:59,390
The alps who attack to the Nökers from
Cengiz's blessed blood.

869
01:59:59,830 --> 02:00:02,360
Your courage is unbelievable.

870
02:00:02,410 --> 02:00:04,610
We've hard that...

871
02:00:04,720 --> 02:00:09,850
Kayıs forgot Mongol's anger in Söğüt.

872
02:00:09,900 --> 02:00:13,320
We have come to remind you
who rules here.

873
02:00:13,320 --> 02:00:15,750
Drown in Cengiz's blood, dog!

874
02:00:25,030 --> 02:00:27,930
Protect us my Allah.

875
02:00:30,310 --> 02:00:32,560
Kill all the Alps!

876
02:00:34,150 --> 02:00:36,880
Kill everyone who resists!

877
02:01:00,340 --> 02:01:02,320
Mongols have come, my Bey.

878
02:01:02,460 --> 02:01:07,110
Why are you running, bre!
Is it appropriate to run from death?

879
02:01:07,140 --> 02:01:10,170
They running like a headless sheep.

880
02:01:10,400 --> 02:01:15,080
Neck or nothing, Sergeant Samsa!

881
02:01:17,480 --> 02:01:20,760
Let's remind them Turk's power.

882
02:01:23,220 --> 02:01:27,450
It has been a long time since I killed one
of them.

883
02:01:27,490 --> 02:01:30,950
It's going to be a fun, Bamsı Bey.

884
02:01:32,290 --> 02:01:34,480
Allah is eternal!

885
02:01:34,820 --> 02:01:36,910
Allah is eternal!

886
02:02:15,490 --> 02:02:19,620
The flag represents Turks' independence.

887
02:02:19,790 --> 02:02:25,340
We break those who intend to harm it.

888
02:02:26,340 --> 02:02:30,880
This is Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman's word.

889
02:02:31,360 --> 02:02:34,280
- Remember this.
- Osman Bey.

890
02:03:12,440 --> 02:03:17,460
- Speaks in an old language -

891
02:03:39,180 --> 02:03:44,280
Turks' Beys are going to fall like rain.

892
02:03:44,590 --> 02:03:48,210
They'll seek mercy.

893
02:03:53,230 --> 02:03:58,290
"May Ovoo bless every stone and tree
with blood."

894
02:04:22,280 --> 02:04:24,170
Kill them all!

895
02:05:37,300 --> 02:05:43,460
Balgay. Osman is standing against our
soldiers with his Alps.

896
02:05:43,530 --> 02:05:47,000
They killed Nökers.

897
02:05:48,760 --> 02:05:50,980
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

898
02:05:50,980 --> 02:05:56,210
Osman smelled us.

899
02:05:57,780 --> 02:06:00,670
The prey is here.

900
02:06:01,160 --> 02:06:03,560
Bring him here at once.

901
02:06:17,320 --> 02:06:19,540
Balgay wants Osman.

902
02:06:26,190 --> 02:06:28,990
Balgay waits for Osman.

903
02:06:29,120 --> 02:06:31,590
Don't mercy whoever resists.

904
02:06:32,700 --> 02:06:37,840
My Osman, what those crickets want
from you?

905
02:06:39,300 --> 02:06:42,010
Let's see what's wrong with Balgay.

906
02:06:42,060 --> 02:06:44,660
Lower your weapon, Osman Bey.

907
02:06:44,860 --> 02:06:47,200
Your Alps, too.

908
02:07:02,310 --> 02:07:04,150
Alps!

909
02:07:08,370 --> 02:07:10,290
Drop your weapon.

910
02:08:12,390 --> 02:08:18,040
My Osman said Alişar's gold is coming from
Konya.

911
02:08:18,040 --> 02:08:23,470
The owner of the gold we took from the
caravanserai is now clear, Bamsı Bey.

912
02:08:24,600 --> 02:08:31,180
They took the gold back. But, it's now clear
that those dogs we killed are Balgay's.

913
02:08:31,260 --> 02:08:33,070
are Balgay's.

914
02:08:33,750 --> 02:08:39,240
It's not about the gold or soldiers.
Balgay has something else in mind.

915
02:08:42,600 --> 02:08:48,070
Caravanserai was raided, and now we know
who is Alişar with.

916
02:08:48,240 --> 02:08:52,030
That's what Osman wanted to reveal.

917
02:08:52,480 --> 02:08:56,910
May Allah bless us with an honorable death,
Bamsı Bey.

918
02:08:57,250 --> 02:09:05,100
May Allah grant us with killing those guys
with our bare hands before we die.

919
02:09:06,170 --> 02:09:11,250
- Amin, brother, amin.
- Eyvallah, son. Eyvallah (may it be).

920
02:09:31,900 --> 02:09:33,410
Sit down.

921
02:09:53,390 --> 02:09:57,370
- Speaks in an old language -

922
02:09:59,010 --> 02:10:03,850
There is always better,
there is always a stronger one.

923
02:10:05,610 --> 02:10:10,830
We have a lot of enemies because of
our manhood.

924
02:10:12,110 --> 02:10:17,680
Your grandfather is Suleyman Shah.
Your father is Ertuğrul Ghazi.

925
02:10:18,600 --> 02:10:20,970
Now, it's you.

926
02:10:25,140 --> 02:10:28,890
My breed goes back to Oguz Kagan.

927
02:10:29,010 --> 02:10:32,580
You can't even count in your lifespan.

928
02:10:33,800 --> 02:10:39,970
If I intend to kill you, I'd spend my
least important...

929
02:10:40,000 --> 02:10:43,760
soldier on you.

930
02:10:44,030 --> 02:10:46,400
If I want to buy you...

931
02:10:47,780 --> 02:10:50,810
Even Cengiz Han's treasures wouldn't be
enough.

932
02:10:52,140 --> 02:10:58,330
Then, give me my sword back so that I
can take your head.

933
02:10:59,590 --> 02:11:07,050
While there are so many heads you'll take,
fights you'll have...

934
02:11:07,080 --> 02:11:10,840
castles you'll conquer...

935
02:11:13,420 --> 02:11:16,030
why would you consider Balgay's head?

936
02:11:17,160 --> 02:11:22,330
I studied you very well, Osman Bey.

937
02:11:25,990 --> 02:11:29,060
How do you think you'll buy me?

938
02:11:29,830 --> 02:11:34,270
By whetting your greed which is as
great as...

939
02:11:34,270 --> 02:11:37,670
the Khan Tengri Mountain...

940
02:11:39,860 --> 02:11:41,870
and as great as Gobi Desert.

941
02:11:53,300 --> 02:11:55,070
Tell me.

942
02:11:57,090 --> 02:11:59,920
Let's just cut to the case.

943
02:12:00,830 --> 02:12:02,830
What do you mean?

944
02:12:03,730 --> 02:12:06,340
Listen to me very carefully, Osman Bey.

945
02:12:08,370 --> 02:12:11,410
I bid you death...

946
02:12:13,840 --> 02:12:16,560
to you and your brothers outside.

947
02:12:19,290 --> 02:12:23,920
By my will, or by fighting.
You choose.

948
02:12:26,510 --> 02:12:32,490
Die now, or be my banner lord.

949
02:12:32,720 --> 02:12:34,980
And shake the whole world.

950
02:12:41,650 --> 02:12:59,260
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com